-- title:
--   Character group of a finite abelian group has the same order
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a type carrying an additive commutative group structure, and assume $M$ is finite. Mathlib's `CharacterModule M` is the group $M \to_{+} \mathrm{AddCircle}\,(1 : \mathbb{Q})$ of additive homomorphisms from $M$ into $\mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}$, the quotient of $\mathbb{Q}$ by the subgroup generated by $1$. The theorem asserts the equality of natural-number cardinalities $\mathrm{Nat.card}\,(\mathrm{CharacterModule}\,M) = \mathrm{Nat.card}\,M$, i.e. the character group $M^{\vee} = \operatorname{Hom}(M, \mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z})$ has exactly as many elements as $M$. No structure on $M$ beyond being a finite abelian group is assumed, and no identification of $M$ with $M^{\vee}$ is asserted: only the counting statement is made.
--
--   This is the counting half of Pontryagin duality for finite abelian groups. It is used in the project to compare cardinalities of quotients by ideals with cardinalities of the corresponding torsion submodules, as in [`CharacterModule.natCard_quotient_ideal_smul_top_eq_natCard_torsionBySet`](thm.html#CharacterModule.natCard_quotient_ideal_smul_top_eq_natCard_torsionBySet) and the subsequent estimates for quotients of modules over reduced rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CharacterModule_natCard_eq_of_finite.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CharacterModule.natCard_eq_of_finite (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Finite M] :
    Nat.card (CharacterModule M) = Nat.card M := by sorry
